# Component Doc Scaffold (编辑前必建目录)

When the user **starts editing a component's documentation** (new or existing nav item without a full item folder), **first** ensure the item directory and media folders exist — then edit markdown.

## Prefer the scaffold command

```bash
pnpm scaffold:doc <sectionId> <slug> "<title>" [--id eds-...] [--preview]
```

Creates all markdown files, `index.ts`, `registry.ts` entry, and media subdirs.

## Manual layout (must match)

```
src/content/docs/{section}/{slug}/
  design.desktop.md / design.mobile.md / design.website.md
  develop.desktop.md / develop.mobile.md / develop.website.md
  index.ts

public/docs/{imageAssetDir}/
  desktop/    ← design.desktop
  mobile/
  website/
  (no develop/ — 开发指南无图形)
```

`imageAssetDir`: atoms → `{slug}`; others → `{section}/{slug}`.

## After scaffold

1. Register in `src/content/docs/registry.ts` (if not using command)
2. Add nav item in `src/config/navigation.ts` → `sectionNavById`
3. Put assets in the **scope folder matching the active Tab** (`!file.png` → `public/docs/.../{scope}/file.png`)

## Do not

- Edit prose before item folder exists
- Put develop-guide media under `public/docs/`

See `src/content/docs/README.md`.
